{
  "screens": [
    {
      "kind": "hookText",
      "text": "Gregor Mendel crossed purple and white pea plants and counted thousands of seeds. Again and again, the white flowers came back in neat, steady shares. How can a mix of seeds be so predictable?",
      "image": null,
      "visual": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "explanation",
      "title": "Passing on one copy",
      "text": "Each plant has two copies of its flower-color code. Each copy is an **allele**: P or p. One P makes a plant purple. Only two p's make it white. Each parent passes on one allele, so Pp × pp gives Pp or pp, half the time each.",
      "exampleLineIdea": "a trait you share with a parent, such as eye color",
      "image": null,
      "visual": null,
      "explore": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "activity",
      "template": "combinationGrid",
      "content": "{\"prompt\":\"Fill in each cell of this Punnett square. Each cell is one possible seed.\",\"fields\":{\"title\":\"Purple Pp × white pp\",\"rule\":\"alleles\",\"columns\":{\"label\":\"Purple parent\",\"values\":[\"P\",\"p\"]},\"rows\":{\"label\":\"White parent\",\"values\":[\"p\",\"p\"]},\"traits\":{\"dominant\":\"Purple\",\"recessive\":\"White\"}},\"check\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"question\":\"Using your square, what share of the seeds grow white flowers?\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"quarter\",\"text\":\"1 in 4\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"That's the share for a cross of two Pp plants. Here the white parent has no P, so more seeds come out white.\"},{\"id\":\"half\",\"text\":\"1 in 2\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"reason\":\"Two of the four cells are pp, and only pp seeds are white. Two out of four is 1 in 2.\"},{\"id\":\"three_quarters\",\"text\":\"3 in 4\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"That's the purple share for a cross of two Pp plants. Here only half the seeds are purple.\"},{\"id\":\"all\",\"text\":\"All of them\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"Only pp seeds are white. The Pp seeds are purple, so not every seed is white.\"}]},\"template\":\"combinationGrid\"}"
    },
    {
      "kind": "activity",
      "template": "randomSimulation",
      "content": "{\"prompt\":\"Each batch is 100 seeds from this cross, and each seed has a 1 in 2 chance of being white.\",\"fields\":{\"mode\":\"chance\",\"hitLabel\":\"White flower\",\"trialLabel\":\"Seed\",\"runs\":1000,\"model\":{\"kind\":\"binomial\",\"trials\":100,\"probability\":0.5,\"hit\":{\"comparison\":\"exactly\",\"value\":50}}},\"check\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"question\":\"Before you run the batches, about how often will a batch have exactly 50 white flowers?\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"most\",\"text\":\"Most of the time\",\"value\":0.6,\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"Batches usually land near 50, but landing exactly on 50 is rare. Only about 8 in 100 batches hit it.\"},{\"id\":\"eight\",\"text\":\"About 8% of batches\",\"value\":0.08,\"isCorrect\":true,\"reason\":\"Exactly 50 white in 100 seeds happens in about 8 of every 100 batches. Batches cluster near 50, but landing on it exactly is uncommon.\"},{\"id\":\"quarter\",\"text\":\"About 25% of batches\",\"value\":0.25,\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"A quarter is too high. Exactly 50 is one count among many possible counts, so it comes up less often than that.\"},{\"id\":\"one\",\"text\":\"About 1% of batches\",\"value\":0.01,\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"That's too low. Exactly 50 is the single most likely count for 100 seeds, so it comes up more than 1 time in 100.\"}]},\"template\":\"randomSimulation\"}"
    },
    {
      "kind": "check",
      "context": "Maya, a gardener in Boise, crosses a purple Pp plant with a white pp plant. Her Punnett square predicts 1 in 2 seeds will grow white. Out of 100 seeds, 47 grow white flowers.",
      "question": "Was the 1 in 2 prediction wrong?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "No, 47 is a normal result for 100 seeds",
          "isCorrect": true,
          "reason": "Batches of 100 often land a few seeds away from 50. Chance spreads results around the predicted share, so 47 fits 1 in 2.",
          "picture": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Yes, 47 is not 50, so the prediction failed",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "47 is close to 50, and one batch often misses by a few seeds. Missing 50 slightly doesn't make the prediction wrong.",
          "picture": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Yes, the seeds must have a different chance than 1 in 2",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "One batch of 47 can't show that. Chance can pull a single batch away from 50, so you'd need many batches to compare.",
          "picture": null
        }
      ],
      "image": null,
      "visual": null,
      "basis": null
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "ideas": [
      {
        "label": "Punnett square: every pairing",
        "text": "A Punnett square lists each parent's alleles along its sides, so every cell is one possible seed."
      },
      {
        "label": "Shares of cells give chances",
        "text": "The share of cells with a trait is the chance that one seed shows that trait."
      },
      {
        "label": "Chance spreads results",
        "text": "Over many batches, results cluster near the predicted share but rarely match it exactly."
      }
    ],
    "shape": "hub"
  }
}

{
  "screens": [
    {
      "kind": "hookText",
      "text": "Uma questão de prova pergunta quanta energia a célula ganha ao quebrar a glicose, o açúcar que você come. A primeira etapa produz 4 moedas de energia. Quanto sobra por glicose, de verdade?",
